natoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">1. The above unaudited consolidated and standalone financial results of the Company for the quarter ended 30th  &lt;br /&gt; 
June 2026 have been reviewed by Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at their respective &lt;br /&gt; 
meetings held on 12th August 2026. &lt;br /&gt; 
2. During the quarter ended 30th June 2026 Hintastica Private Limited HPL transitioned from a 50 50 joint &lt;br /&gt; 
venture with Atlantic Societe Francaise de Developpement Thermique France Atlantic to a wholly owned &lt;br /&gt; 
subsidiary after the Company fully subscribed to its Rs.15 crore share of a rights issue on 4th June 2026 raising &lt;br /&gt; 
its stake to 96.6 percent as Atlantic did not participate and subsequently acquired Atlantics remaining 3.4 percent stake on 30th June 2026. Accordingly HPL was consolidated as a subsidiary effective 4th June 2026. &lt;br /&gt; 
3. Exceptional Items &lt;br /&gt; 
a. Based on an independent valuation during the quarter ended 30th June 2026 the Company restated its &lt;br /&gt; 
investment in HPL under Exceptional Items recognizing a Rs.0.14 crore impairment loss in the Standalone  &lt;br /&gt; 
financial results and a Rs.0.83 crore impairment loss reversal in the Consolidated financial results. &lt;br /&gt; 
b. To optimize focus on its core kitchen appliance business the Board approved exiting high-loss product &lt;br /&gt; 
categories air purifiers water purifiers furniture fittings fans and non ecommerce air coolers on 12th August 2025.  &lt;br /&gt; 
This exit resulted in a net exceptional charge of Rs.44.28 crore for FY 2025 26 initially provided at Rs.49.49 crore in  &lt;br /&gt; 
Ql FY 2025 26 and offset by asset disposal reversals of Rs.0.61 crore in Q2 FY 2025 26 and Rs.4.60 crore in Q3 FY 2025 26. &lt;br /&gt; 
4. On 27th March 2025 the Board approved a Composite Scheme of Arrangement effective 1st April 2025 to &lt;br /&gt; 
